ed]]\n*1 white [[Cookbook:Turnip|turnip]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n*3 stalks [[Cookbook:Celery|celery]], chopped\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n*[[Cookbook:Pepper|Pepper]]\n*Ground [[Cookbook:Clove|cloves]]\n*[[Cookbook:Tumeric|Turmeric]]\n*[[Cookbook:Nutmeg|Nutmeg]]\n*[[Cookbook:Cumin|Cumin]]\n*[[Cookbook:Curry Powder|Curry powder]]\n*[[Cookbook:Cornstarch|Cornstarch]]\n*[[Cookbook:Sour Cream|Sour cream]], as a garnish\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Add the split peas to a pot. Add the chicken broth and enough water to cover the peas.\n# Bring the peas to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]], then remove from the heat and let soak.\n# Prepare equal quantities of grated carrot and chopped onion.\n# Add the carrot, onion, turnip, and celery to the split peas. Mix in salt, pepper, cloves, turmeric, nutmeg, cumin, and curry powder.\n# [[Cookbook:Simmering|Simmer]] everything slowly for about an hour, or until the vegetables are well softened. Adjust seasoning to taste.\n# Make a mixture of cornstarch and water with the consistency of thin cream.\n# Bring the split peas to a simmer. Mix in the cornstarch slurry, and cook for a minute or two until thickened.\n# Adjust the consistency with stock (or milk) as desired.\n# Serve hot. If desired, garnish with a floating dab of sour cream and a light sprinkling of nutmeg.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using split peas]]\n[[Category:Recipes for soup]]\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using clove]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cornstarch]]\n[[Category:Recipes using curry powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cumin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Purée Mongole","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 lb dry split peas","sourceText":"1 lb dry split peas","amountText":"1 lb dry split peas","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"Water","sourceText":"Water","